---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { repository } from "../../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ScreenRecorder troubleshooting"
  description="Use recording diagnostics and common checks to troubleshoot ScreenRecorder capture and encoding problems."
>
  <article class="guide wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/docs/">← All documentation</a><div
      class="eyebrow"
    >
      HELP · 4 MIN READ
    </div><h1>
      When a recording<br /><span class="accent-word">needs a hand.</span>
    </h1><p class="guide-lead">
      Start with the output file and diagnostic sidecar, then include useful
      details if you need help from the project.
    </p><h2>Windows diagnostics</h2><p>
      Each recording writes a timestamped diagnostics file under <code
        >&lt;recording folder&gt;\_diagnostics</code
      >. It includes capture and encoder settings, errors, pipeline progress,
      output size, and stop/finalize stages.
    </p><ul class="guide-list">
      <li>
        If an MP4 is missing, check for a <code>.partial.mp4</code> file and review
        the diagnostic sidecar.
      </li><li>
        If the app stops making progress, note the last completed pipeline or
        shutdown stage.
      </li><li>
        Check that the destination drive has enough free space and that the
        folder is writable.
      </li><li>
        If a microphone or desktop audio is missing, verify the selected Windows
        input/output devices and app settings.
      </li>
    </ul><h2>Fedora checks</h2><ul class="guide-list">
      <li>
        Confirm you are using GNOME on Wayland and that the desktop portal
        prompt was completed.
      </li><li>
        Check that the selected display/window and audio devices are still
        available.
      </li><li>
        For RPM install problems, review the DNF output and use an RPM matching
        your machine architecture.
      </li>
    </ul><h2>Report a problem</h2><p>
      Include your operating system, ScreenRecorder version, steps to reproduce,
      and relevant diagnostic text. Review logs for personal information before
      sharing.
    </p><a
      class="button button-primary"
      href={`${repository}/issues`}
      target="_blank"
      rel="noreferrer">Open a GitHub issue ↗</a>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
